  "aiOverview": {
    "content": "Yes, a 16-seed has beaten a 1-seed in the men's NCAA tournament twice since the field expanded in 1985. The historic upsets were pulled off by UMBC against Virginia in 2018 (74-54) and Fairleigh Dickinson against Purdue in 2023 (63-58). Entering 2026, 1-seeds are 158-2 against 16-seeds. Key 16-Seed Over 1-Seed Upsets: 2018: UMBC became the first-ever 16-seed to defeat a 1-seed, stunning top-seeded Virginia 74-54. 2023: Fairleigh Dickinson became the second 16-seed to win, upsetting Purdue 63-58. In the women's tournament, a 16-seed has also won once, when Harvard defeated top-seeded Stanford in 1998.",
